Data intensity: Relies on high-resolution order-message data and accurate timestamps, which may vary across venues.

No profit verification: The model quantifies potential gain but does not confirm actual arbitrage profits.

Calibration sensitivity: Choice of thresholds for capacity outliers and latency impact can materially affect alert frequency.

Opaque parameters: Public exchange-capacity estimates may not fully reflect proprietary infrastructure or dynamic bandwidth changes.

